---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
const repo = "https://github.com/tidus747/planacity";
const later = [
  [
    "v0.6",
    "Milestones & Deliveries",
    "Represent program outcomes, readiness dependencies, and delivery risk.",
  ],
  [
    "v0.7",
    "Communication",
    "Share timelines, capacity, calendars, and a Program Pack outside the application.",
  ],
  [
    "v0.8",
    "Scenarios & Reconciliation",
    "Compare alternatives and reconcile Jira re-imports without losing the baseline.",
  ],
  [
    "v0.9",
    "Stabilisation",
    "Focus on reliability, performance, keyboard access, migrations, and installers.",
  ],
  [
    "v1.0",
    "A dependable planning loop",
    "Import, structure, schedule, allocate, validate, communicate, and export.",
  ],
];
---

<Page
  title="Roadmap"
  description="The Planacity roadmap: reliable planning, explainable capacity, team visibility, and small, reviewable releases."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE ROAD AHEAD</p>
      <h1>
        Small releases.
        <br />
        Useful progress.
      </h1>
      <p>
        A clear direction, shaped by real planning work. Each step should make
        one more part of the program easier to understand.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="doc-grid">
      <aside class="doc-nav" aria-label="Roadmap sections">
        <p>In this roadmap</p>
        <a href="#available">Available today</a>
        <a href="#current">v0.5 / Current focus</a>
        <a href="#next">v0.5 / Next slices</a>
        <a href="#later">Beyond the preview</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>Track GitHub issues</a>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="notice">
          <strong>Current target: v0.5 Program Calendar</strong>
          <p>
            This is a development preview, not a published stable release. The
            roadmap describes direction, not promised delivery dates.
          </p>
        </div>
        <section id="available">
          <h2>A working foundation</h2>
          <p>Available in the source preview:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Local project files, JSON backups, a hierarchical Plan editor, and
              filters.
            </li>
            <li>
              Jira CSV import/export, field mappings, and imported baseline
              comparison. Additive imports can use existing references as
              hierarchy anchors, and Plan identifies baseline-backed work.
            </li>
            <li>
              Timeline scales, grouping, filters, dependency arrows, Team mode,
              a selected-work graph, critical-path analysis, and date editing.
            </li>
            <li>
              People, work calendars, dated availability, recurring duties,
              one-person executable-work assignments, and exact capacity views.
            </li>
            <li>
              Shared program events in Calendar, Overview, and Timeline, plus a
              reviewed generic availability CSV import workflow.
            </li>
            <li>
              First-class sprints with manual Calendar editing and explicit
              assignment of executable leaf work.
            </li>
            <li>
              Estimate units in hours, days, or weeks, with calendar setup in
              the same dialog.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            These foundations are implemented in the source preview. Jira
            re-import reconciliation, automatic sprint distribution, and a
            stable installer are not yet available.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="current">
          <h2>Now: keep capacity and Jira traceability consistent.</h2>
          <p>
            Development proceeds through focused issues, one at a time. The
            source version remains 0.4.0.dev0 until a release change is
            reviewed.
          </p>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.5 A</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Team visibility - complete</h3>
              <p>
                Team Timeline lanes, availability overlays, dependency cards,
                stable work identity, and critical-path analysis are available.
              </p>
              <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md`}>
                Review the detailed roadmap
              </a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.5 B</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Program Calendar - complete in source</h3>
              <p>
                The shared-event domain and persistence introduced in schema
                12, capacity effects, Calendar editor, Overview summary, and
                optional Timeline lanes are complete. Generic availability CSV
                import is reviewed in Calendar before it changes the plan.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">v0.5 C</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Manual sprint planning - foundation complete</h3>
              <p>
                Schema 13 stores first-class sprints and leaf assignments.
                Calendar supports explicit creation, editing, assignment,
                reassignment, and diagnostics without moving work dates.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">ACTIVE</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Reservation-backed Jira work</h3>
              <p>
                The explicit allocation-to-reservation domain link and schema
                14 persistence lifecycle are in place. Exact capacity now
                separates covered, excess, and unused hours, while Plan and
                People provide explicit person-compatible manual editing.
                Optional CSV mapping and shared visual findings remain focused
                slices of issue #161.
              </p>
              <a href={`${repo}/issues/161`}>Follow issue #161</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>
        <section id="next">
          <h2>Next: deepen the v0.5 planning loop.</h2>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">SPRINTS</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Sprint capacity and load</h3>
              <p>
                Compare assigned sprint demand with group capacity and preserve
                work outside sprints or crossing their boundaries as explicit
                findings. Automatic distribution remains a later reviewed
                proposal, not a silent mutation.
              </p>
              <a href={`${repo}/issues/147`}>Follow issue #147</a>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">IMPORTS</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Factorial exported files</h3>
              <p>
                Adapt exported files to the same reviewed import workflow. Keep
                provider terminology outside the canonical planning model and
                avoid storing unnecessary HR detail.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="release">
            <span class="release-tag">GUIDE</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Offline planning-assistant guide</h3>
              <p>
                Package the versioned schema guidance and expose it through Help
                without accounts, automatic uploads, or a provider dependency.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>
        <section id="later">
          <h2>Beyond the preview</h2>
          {later.map(([version, title, description]) => (
            <article class="release">
              <span class="release-tag">{version}</span>
              <div>
                <h3>{title}</h3>
                <p>{description}</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </section>
        <div class="notice">
          <strong>Follow the decisions, not just the feature list.</strong>
          <p>
            The{" "}
            <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md`}>
              implementation roadmap
            </a>{" "}
            defines issue scope and acceptance.{" "}
            <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/planning-decisions.md`}>
              Planning decisions
            </a>{" "}
            explain calculation rules and data integrity. Live progress belongs
            in <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>GitHub Issues</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Page>
